<BaseLayout title="Start Blue | Franco Lopez" description="Start Blue is LS Tractor's official tractor quoting platform for the U.S. and Canada, running on Kubernetes and used by customers and 350+ dealerships.">
  <header class="page-header">
    <span class="eyebrow">production platform · 350+ dealerships</span>
    <h1>Start Blue</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      LS Tractor's official tractor quoting platform for the U.S. and Canada: open to the public, with
      secure accounts for 350+ dealerships.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="https://startblue.lstractorusa.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit platform</a>
      <a class="button" href="/blog/dev/start-blue-lessons-from-a-dealer-quote-platform/">What it taught me</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <article class="content">
    <h2>Problem</h2>
    <p>
      Dealer quotes depended on spreadsheets, PDFs, and a lot of manual work. It worked, but it wasn't
      consistent, and keeping pricing current across hundreds of dealers was hard.
    </p>

    <h2>What I built</h2>
    <p>
      I designed, built, and operate Start Blue. It holds the full tractor inventory and configurations, so
      anyone can configure a tractor and get a quote in a few clicks. Dealerships sign in with their own
      accounts to save quotes and apply their own pricing. More than 3,000 quotes have been generated.
    </p>

    <h2>Architecture</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>React frontend, Django backend, and PostgreSQL, with object storage for files</li>
      <li>Three-node Kubernetes cluster on Linode/Akamai</li>
      <li>GitOps delivery: GitHub Actions builds images, Flux CD reconciles the cluster from Git</li>
      <li>SOPS for encrypted secrets in the repository</li>
      <li>Traefik and cert-manager for ingress and automated TLS certificates</li>
      <li>Automated restic backups of application data and cluster configuration</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Operational concerns</h2>
    <p>
      Writing the application was only part of the job. I also own the container images, deployments,
      backups, PostgreSQL, monitoring, DNS, and TLS. Running a database inside Kubernetes means planning
      for persistent data, backups, and schema changes, not just restarting containers.
    </p>

    <h2>Impact</h2>
    <p>
      Start Blue has been in production for over two years without a major incident. I presented it at
      LS Mtron's headquarters in South Korea, including to the Global CEO, and the work was recognized
      with the 2025 CEO Award for Employee of the Year. I'm now working with engineering teams there to
      adapt it for multiple languages and other global markets.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
